# Table Display — No Scrollbars

For complicated data tables (e.g. `.activity-section`, `.history-section`, transaction logs, audit tables), **do not show scrollbars**. Users can still scroll horizontally via touch, trackpad, or mouse drag.

## Reference Elements

- `main#main-content > div#dashboard > div.activity-section` — Recent Activity table
- `main#main-content > div.history-section` — Minting Audit Log table

## Implementation

### 1. No Vertical Scrollbar

- Do **not** use `max-height` + `overflow-y: auto` on the table wrapper.
- Let the section height grow to fit all rows.

### 2. No Horizontal Scrollbar

On the table wrapper (e.g. `.activity-table-wrap`, `.history-table-wrap`):

```css
.table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    scrollbar-width: none;
    -ms-overflow-style: none;
}
.table-wrap::-webkit-scrollbar {
    display: none;
}
```

- `scrollbar-width: none` — Firefox
- `-ms-overflow-style: none` — IE/Edge
- `::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none }` — Chrome, Safari

Content remains horizontally scrollable; only the scrollbar is hidden.

## Apply To

- Any new table with many columns or rows that might overflow
- Existing tables when adding similar patterns
